.TH "LMM" "1" "Jul 2026" "lmm 2.0.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
lmm-snapshot-create - Record the current arrangement under a name


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm snapshot create [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Record the current arrangement of a game and profile under a name.

.PP
Without --name the snapshot is named after the moment it was taken. A name
already in use is refused rather than overwritten - a snapshot is the only
copy of an arrangement you asked lmm to remember.

.PP
Examples:
  lmm snapshot create --game skyrim-se
  lmm snapshot create --game skyrim-se --name before-total-conversion
  lmm snapshot create --game skyrim-se --profile survival --name known-good


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	name for the snapshot (default: the current date and time)

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to record (default: active profile)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lmm or ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/lmm or ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output JSON instead of text; mutating commands print their result, --dry-run prints the plan; never prompts

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="off"
	diagnostic log level written to stderr (off, error, warn, info, debug)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
